WEBVTT

1
00:00:26.083 --> 00:00:29.916


2
00:00:29.916 --> 00:00:33.166
<b>Seeing his loved ones</b>
<b>all around him in the battlefield, </b>

3
00:00:33.166 --> 00:00:36.833
<b>Arjuna's physical state became unsteady,</b>

4
00:00:36.833 --> 00:00:38.666
<b>his hands began to tremble.</b>

5
00:00:38.666 --> 00:00:40.000
<b>He says,</b>

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:41.166
<b>"O Keshava,</b>

7
00:00:41.166 --> 00:00:44.583
<b>I am unable to stand steady, </b>

8
00:00:44.583 --> 00:00:47.791
<b>my mind is also becoming confused, </b>

9
00:00:47.791 --> 00:00:51.375
<b>all these signs seem adverse to me."</b>

10
00:00:52.083 --> 00:00:56.291


11
00:00:56.291 --> 00:00:59.875
<b>Arjuna prepared for this war for many years,</b>

12
00:00:59.875 --> 00:01:03.166
<b>entering it thinking he would be victorious </b>

13
00:01:03.166 --> 00:01:05.125
<b>and destroy the unrighteous. </b>

14
00:01:05.125 --> 00:01:09.833
<b>He came to the middle of the battlefield to see</b>
<b>the faces of those very unrighteous ones, </b>

15
00:01:09.833 --> 00:01:11.083
<b>but now? </b>

16
00:01:11.083 --> 00:01:11.750
<b>Now </b>

17
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:15.916
<b>suddenly every sign seems contrary.</b>

18
00:01:15.916 --> 00:01:17.625
<b>His body was becoming unstable,</b>

19
00:01:17.625 --> 00:01:21.083
<b>and now even his mind has</b>
<b>become uncontrolled. </b>

20
00:01:21.083 --> 00:01:23.625
<b>Is this what war is?</b>

21
00:01:23.625 --> 00:01:26.875
<b>Is this how one strikes down</b>
<b>their own loved ones?</b>

22
00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:30.958
<b>Whatever he had thought,</b>
<b>this is completely opposite to that.</b>

23
00:01:30.958 --> 00:01:31.666
<b>But</b>

24
00:01:31.666 --> 00:01:35.250
<b>is this truth really contrary</b>
<b>to what he had thought?</b>

25
00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:36.250
<b>But if not,</b>

26
00:01:36.250 --> 00:01:38.875
<b>the preparation for war had</b>
<b>been going on for years,</b>

27
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:40.000
<b>it was also known</b>

28
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.375
<b>that destruction happens in war,</b>

29
00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:45.208
<b>and it was known who the war was against. </b>

30
00:01:45.208 --> 00:01:47.083
<b>So how is this moment contrary?</b>

31
00:01:47.083 --> 00:01:49.791
<b>This was indeed certain.</b>

32
00:01:49.791 --> 00:01:50.625
<b>Here</b>

33
00:01:50.625 --> 00:01:53.583
<b>Arjuna addresses Krishna as Keshava.</b>

34
00:01:53.583 --> 00:01:57.875
<b>Keshava means the slayer of the demon Keshi.</b>

35
00:01:57.875 --> 00:01:59.208
<b>It's as if he's saying,</b>

36
00:01:59.208 --> 00:02:04.541
<b>"Krishna, you ended the life of the</b>
<b>terrible demon named Keshi,</b>

37
00:02:04.541 --> 00:02:09.125
<b>now please end this confusion</b>
<b>in my mind as well."</b>

38
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:13.791


39
00:02:13.791 --> 00:02:15.291
<b>O Keshava!</b>

40
00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:21.458
<b>Everything seems contrary.</b>

41
00:02:21.458 --> 00:02:24.916
<b>Arjuna is a great warrior,</b>

42
00:02:24.916 --> 00:02:27.500
<b>he has fought many battles.</b>

43
00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.833
<b>He knew who the unrighteous were,</b>

44
00:02:29.833 --> 00:02:34.041
<b>he also knew what happens in war.</b>

45
00:02:34.041 --> 00:02:37.791
<b>Here, Arjuna is forgetting everything.</b>

46
00:02:37.791 --> 00:02:39.875
<b>He's forgetting Draupadi's insult,</b>

47
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:42.541
<b>the Kauravas' deceit and trickery,</b>

48
00:02:42.541 --> 00:02:45.500
<b>forgetting that</b>

49
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:52.750
<b>Duryodhana was eager to take the Pandavas'</b>
<b>lives in the house of lac.</b>

50
00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.666
<b>I will certainly take care of Arjuna,</b>

51
00:02:55.666 --> 00:02:58.166
<b>and I say to you as well.</b>

52
00:02:58.166 --> 00:03:00.000
<b>Mind.</b>

53
00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:02.916
<b>We greatly underestimate</b>
<b>the strength of the mind.</b>

54
00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:05.166
<b>If you are the master of your mind,</b>

55
00:03:05.166 --> 00:03:07.125
<b>you can conquer the world,</b>

56
00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:10.583
<b>but if the mind overpowers you,</b>

57
00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:16.166
<b>even a great warrior like Arjuna admits</b>
<b>defeat before even lifting his weapon. </b>

58
00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:20.625
<b>And what's more, this trembling of Arjuna's body?</b>

59
00:03:20.625 --> 00:03:24.958
<b>This too is the mind's doing.</b>

60
00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:31.875
<b>An unsettled mind creates weaknesses</b>
<b>in the body, creates diseases.</b>

61
00:03:31.875 --> 00:03:34.666
<b>And on the other hand, a stable mind? </b>

62
00:03:34.666 --> 00:03:36.833
<b>You'll find many examples</b>

63
00:03:36.833 --> 00:03:38.333
<b>where doctors</b>

64
00:03:38.333 --> 00:03:43.250
<b>and specialists have given up,</b>
<b>saying there's no cure for this disease, </b>

65
00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.041
<b>but</b>

66
00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:48.041
<b> a person with a stable and strong mind</b>

67
00:03:48.041 --> 00:03:52.666
<b>has defeated even cancer with willpower alone.</b>

68
00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:56.875
<b>Astonishing all doctors and specialists.</b>

69
00:03:56.875 --> 00:03:58.541
<b>Mind! </b>

70
00:03:58.541 --> 00:04:01.583
<b>The power of the mind is the supreme power.</b>

71
00:04:02.083 --> 00:04:06.208


72
00:04:06.208 --> 00:04:12.208
<b>At this moment, Arjuna feels that</b>
<b>he is about to make a mistake, </b>

73
00:04:12.208 --> 00:04:13.333
<b>or</b>

74
00:04:13.333 --> 00:04:17.000
<b>that this war itself is wrong. </b>

75
00:04:17.000 --> 00:04:18.791
<b>I know</b>

76
00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:22.208
<b>that this war of Mahabharata is right. </b>

77
00:04:22.208 --> 00:04:23.625
<b>Because, </b>

78
00:04:23.625 --> 00:04:26.666
<b>if unrighteousness is not stopped,</b>

79
00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:30.791
<b>it will grow like cancer. </b>

80
00:04:30.791 --> 00:04:33.958
<b>If Draupadi's insult is forgiven,</b>

81
00:04:33.958 --> 00:04:36.583
<b>what will happen to others? </b>

82
00:04:36.583 --> 00:04:40.000
<b>If the Pandavas'</b>
<b>righteous wife's modesty is not safe, </b>

83
00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.791
<b>will any other mother or daughter</b>
<b>in the kingdom be safe? </b>

84
00:04:45.791 --> 00:04:48.458
<b>And this is not just one instance,</b>

85
00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:52.791
<b>there were many such examples</b>
<b>of Duryodhana's unrighteousness. </b>

86
00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:56.333
<b>The destruction of such</b>
<b>unrighteousness is absolutely right.</b>

87
00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:57.416
<b>When it comes to </b>

88
00:04:57.416 --> 00:04:58.458
<b> family,</b>

89
00:04:58.458 --> 00:04:59.333
<b> society, </b>

90
00:04:59.333 --> 00:05:01.750
<b>community.</b>

91
00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.625
<b>How should decisions be made?</b>

92
00:05:04.625 --> 00:05:08.125
<b>Often there are disagreements in the family. </b>

93
00:05:08.125 --> 00:05:08.916
<b>Or</b>

94
00:05:08.916 --> 00:05:11.166
<b> with some people in the community.</b>

95
00:05:11.166 --> 00:05:11.916
<b>Or</b>

96
00:05:11.916 --> 00:05:15.041
<b>in the neighborhood where we live.</b>

97
00:05:15.041 --> 00:05:16.500
<b>We think</b>

98
00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:17.708
<b>we are right?</b>

99
00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:19.083
<b>And they are wrong. </b>

100
00:05:19.083 --> 00:05:21.041
<b>They feel the same way.</b>

101
00:05:21.041 --> 00:05:28.583
<b>When we view any family/social situation</b>
<b> from this narrow perspective, </b>

102
00:05:28.583 --> 00:05:31.333
<b>the conflict keeps growing.</b>

103
00:05:31.333 --> 00:05:35.958
<b>A clamor begins about who is right, who is right.</b>

104
00:05:35.958 --> 00:05:39.625
<b>And in this noise, we forget, </b>

105
00:05:39.625 --> 00:05:42.375
<b>what is right?</b>

106
00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.125
<b>What is right,</b>

107
00:05:44.125 --> 00:05:46.625
<b>this is the precise question.</b>

108
00:05:46.625 --> 00:05:49.000
<b>Who is right/who is wrong,</b>

109
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:51.333
<b>this question itself is futile.</b>

110
00:05:51.333 --> 00:05:54.541
<b>In any social or family dispute.</b>

111
00:05:54.541 --> 00:05:57.291
<b>Don't think about who is right, </b>

112
00:05:57.291 --> 00:06:01.291
<b>think about what is right.</b>

113
00:06:01.291 --> 00:06:04.291
<b>Because when we think from this perspective,</b>

114
00:06:04.291 --> 00:06:07.208
<b>we will think about the welfare of all, </b>

115
00:06:07.208 --> 00:06:13.000
<b>we will be able to present our</b>
<b>argument properly while respecting everyone,</b>

116
00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:15.875
<b>we will be able to make others understand.</b>

117
00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:20.625


118
00:06:20.625 --> 00:06:24.541
<b>Arjuna calls me Keshava</b>

119
00:06:24.541 --> 00:06:29.500
<b>because I slayed the demon Keshi.</b>

120
00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.541
<b>But here,</b>

121
00:06:31.541 --> 00:06:33.041
<b>Arjuna</b>

122
00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:37.833
<b>might have to slay his own family members.</b>

123
00:06:37.833 --> 00:06:43.083
<b>These two situations are entirely different. </b>

124
00:06:43.083 --> 00:06:46.416
<b>You feel the same, don't you?</b>

125
00:06:46.416 --> 00:06:50.250
<b>That there's a world of difference between</b>
<b>the demon Keshi and the Kauravas.</b>

126
00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:55.666
<b>We are getting stuck on the names</b>
<b>of characters here.</b>

127
00:06:55.666 --> 00:06:58.291
<b>When we look beyond the characters</b>

128
00:06:58.291 --> 00:07:02.125
<b>and view it from the perspective</b>

129
00:07:02.125 --> 00:07:04.458
<b>everything will become clear.</b>

130
00:07:04.458 --> 00:07:09.583
<b>It's not about Keshi demon or the Kauravas.</b>

131
00:07:09.583 --> 00:07:14.916
<b>It's about righteousness and unrighteousness.</b>

132
00:07:14.916 --> 00:07:22.375
<b>In your professional life, you might be</b>
<b>leading a group or an organization. </b>

133
00:07:22.375 --> 00:07:24.083
<b>What should be done</b>

134
00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:26.750
<b>when the path isn't clear?</b>

135
00:07:26.750 --> 00:07:30.708
<b>Just think about two things: </b>

136
00:07:30.708 --> 00:07:33.250
<b>what is your responsibility, </b>

137
00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:37.041
<b>and what is righteous.</b>

138
00:07:37.041 --> 00:07:38.583
<b>If your responsibility</b>

139
00:07:38.583 --> 00:07:42.000
<b>is to advance an enterprise,</b>

140
00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:49.958
<b>and if a particular individual, despite your help,</b>
<b>is continuously failing in their work, </b>

141
00:07:49.958 --> 00:07:54.041
<b>pulling back the progress of that enterprise.</b>

142
00:07:54.041 --> 00:07:54.791
<b>But</b>

143
00:07:54.791 --> 00:07:58.041
<b>hey have a very humble nature.</b>

144
00:07:58.041 --> 00:08:00.541
<b>What would you do in such a situation?</b>

145
00:08:00.541 --> 00:08:05.083
<b>Look at this as a small Mahabharata.</b>

146
00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:06.458
<b>What is right,</b>

147
00:08:06.458 --> 00:08:08.708
<b>regarding your responsibility? </b>

148
00:08:08.708 --> 00:08:12.250
<b>Regarding your duty?</b>

149
00:08:12.250 --> 00:08:15.958
<b>Being sensitive is a good thing,</b>

150
00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:17.125
<b>but</b>

151
00:08:17.125 --> 00:08:19.000
<b>if that very sensitivity</b>

152
00:08:19.000 --> 00:08:21.125
<b>leads you astray from your responsibility, </b>

153
00:08:21.125 --> 00:08:24.250
<b>how can it be right?</b>

